A cliff section in the Bakassi area shows the following, from bottom to top:

- granite **G** at the base;
- on an irregular eroded surface of the granite, beds of sandstone **S**, which are tilted and dip at 30 degrees;
- a fault **F** that displaces the granite and the sandstone but stops at the surface above the tilted sandstone;
- on a second erosion surface across the tilted sandstone, horizontal beds of conglomerate **C**, which contain pebbles of granite and of sandstone;
- a vertical basalt dyke **D** that cuts through G, S and C.

(a) Give the order of the geological events, from oldest to youngest. (b) Name the type of contact between G and S and between S and C. (c) What does the presence of granite pebbles in C show?
